  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bijdrage aan de algemene middelen van het IMF Institute for Capacity Development voor de periode (2021-2024)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The IMF Institute for Capacity Development is a multi-partner organization established to integrate the IMF&apos;s fiscal capacity development operations. This initiative combines under one roof the IMF&apos;s leading global expertise on domestic revenue mobilization, public spending, and public financial management. The Global Public Finance Partnership (GPFP) aims to strengthen the IMF&apos;s capacity development delivery to its member countries, particularly in response to a rapidly increasing demand for support on public finances. The GPFP initiative targets a budget of US$175&#x2013;200 million over five years and is set to be officially launched in mid-2024. The GPFP will be guided by a steering committee that includes representatives from the Contributors and the IMF, providing strategic guidance and setting priorities for the workplan. The activities financed under the Subaccount are technical assistance, training, and related activities of the IMF, governed by the Instrument for a Framework Administered Account for Selected Fund Activities (SFA Framework Instrument). The IMF will identify and employ personnel for the activities under the Subaccount, while goods and services will be procured in accordance with the IMF&apos;s guidelines and procedures. The GPFP is part of a voluntary pluriannual contribution to international multi-partner organizations, with funding from the IMF adm acc (IMF administrative account) and DGD (Directorate-General for Development). The initiative falls under the sector of Government and civil society. Public finance management, within the top sector of Government and civil society (151xx).</narrative>
  </description>
